            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="0971" n="857" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg857"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stockton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-02T17:00:00+01:00">September 2, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 2—3:24 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[40.] My telegram No. 38, August 29, 4 p.m. Schüller has confirmed in informal
                    memorandum Austrian Government’s position proposing <pb facs="0972" n="858"
                        xml:id="pg858"/> exchange of notes to contain reservation and 4–year term
                    from exchange of ratifications, apparently assuming that ratifications could be
                    exchanged about February. He reiterates that Austrian Government’s desire to
                    shorten term is independent of ultimate fate of Senate reservation, apparently
                    meaning whether Senate should withdraw or Austrian Parliament should fail to
                    approve reservation. He has however twice assured me that reservation was
                    immaterial to Austrian Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
